   ],
   "x": "Total subsidies are about 8.5 per cent of Union expenditure in 2026-27; the major subsidy heads are food, fertiliser and petroleum (LPG)."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "id": "g21e0f79303d6",
   "lines": [
    "105:9:4"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 100,
   "sec": 4,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Largest share (15th FC, 2021-26):** **Uttar Pradesh** (about 17.9%), followed by Bihar (about 10.1%)."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 101,
   "sec": 2,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Grant dependence:** panchayats have limited powers to tax, so they depend substantially on **grants** (FC, SFC and CSS funds)."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 102,
   "sec": 0,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- Non-plan expenditure also included **subsidies** (food, fertiliser) and pensions."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 103,
   "sec": 0,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Internal vs external debt:** classified by the **source** of borrowing. Internal debt is borrowed within the country (domestic economy); external debt comes from foreign sources, and foreign-currency obligations belong to it."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 105,
   "sec": 1,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Progressive taxation:** the tax rate rises as income rises, so the rich pay more; this reduces inequality (distribution function)."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 105,
   "sec": 4,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Headline marker:** the **fiscal deficit** is the headline marker of fiscal health; revenue deficit and effective revenue deficit show what the borrowing is used for."
  },
  {
   "book": 3,
   "row": 105,
   "sec": 8,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **FRBM amendment 2018:** made **debt** the anchor with the **fiscal deficit** as the operational target, and **dropped the revenue deficit targets**."
  }
 ],
 "doubtful": []
}